    "detailed_description": "Close the cockpit of your fighter, start the engine and take off. In the story mission, you will have to reliably cover your comrade in the course of a combat mission.<br />\r\nRealism like never before!<br />\r\nA fighter is a complex machine, with its own systems and features, which you have to master in order to successfully complete the task.<br />\r\nNo more speed and distance limits. There are boundless expanses of outer space around. Feel what the cosmic scale really is.<br />\r\nFlying in space is a real test for a pilot. Huge overloads will push in all directions. You will have to maneuver correctly to gain an advantage over the enemy and win, and not lose sight and be destroyed.<br />\r\nA fully clickable cockpit allows you to better immerse yourself in the process of controlling a fighter.<br />\r\nThe Newtonian physics of flight is reproduced with maximum accuracy, which allows for orbital flights and maneuvering.",
    "about_the_game": "Close the cockpit of your fighter, start the engine and take off. In the story mission, you will have to reliably cover your comrade in the course of a combat mission.<br />\r\nRealism like never before!<br />\r\nA fighter is a complex machine, with its own systems and features, which you have to master in order to successfully complete the task.<br />\r\nNo more speed and distance limits. There are boundless expanses of outer space around. Feel what the cosmic scale really is.<br />\r\nFlying in space is a real test for a pilot. Huge overloads will push in all directions. You will have to maneuver correctly to gain an advantage over the enemy and win, and not lose sight and be destroyed.<br />\r\nA fully clickable cockpit allows you to better immerse yourself in the process of controlling a fighter.<br />\r\nThe Newtonian physics of flight is reproduced with maximum accuracy, which allows for orbital flights and maneuvering.",
    "short_description": "Leaving the formation is a story-driven sci-fi combat simulation based on honest Newtonian flight physics.",
